spec.text:
{
 "id": "T-305",
 "milestone": "M2",
 "depends_on": [
  "T-303",
  "T-304"
 ],
 "title": "Every project, external repositories included, decides each task's door from its own sensitive list plus a shared base list, and a task whose door cannot be decided waits on a captain card",
 "public_title": "Two-way and one-way paths for every project",
 "door": {
  "kind": "one-way",
  "reason": "It changes pin records and the per-project config, which are on the sensitive list."
 },
 "scope": [
  "bin/**",
  "skills/**",
  "tests/**",
  "design/design.md",
  "config.yaml",
  "i18n/**"
 ],
 "acceptance": [
  "Why. T-303 decides two-way or one-way only for this repository. On 2026-10-13 the captain set the rule that every project, external repositories included, must be able to decide each task's door, and that firstmate asks the captain whenever it cannot decide.",
  "What, where the lists live. Each external project has its own sensitive list under projects.<name>.door.sensitive. Firstmate proposes the list on a captain card when the project is registered or first needs one, and only an approved card writes it. The engine keeps a base list that applies to every project and that no project can remove: CI and workflow configuration, migrations, SQL files, environment files and secrets folders.",
  "What, the external task. An external spec carries the same door as a self spec, and its pin keeps the effective door. Firstmate's own steps follow the door: the plan round, firstmate's fail-first gate, the review depth it asks its own reviewer for, and the pin stop. The company's reviewers, the external repository's CI and its branch rules stay as they are; firstmate never relaxes a check it does not own.",
  "What, cannot decide means ask. A captain card holds the pin, naming the path or signal that caused it, in en and zh-TW, when: the spec names no door or a malformed one; the project has no approved sensitive list; a changed path matches nothing the lists can classify (a new top-level folder, a renamed file, a submodule); or the signals disagree (the spec says two-way but the diff touches a listed path, or a worker reports a door change). A scope entry wider than a listed path does not by itself raise a card; the diff check covers it, as in T-303.",
  "What, unchanged. Tasks pinned before this change keep their current path until their next repin; a repin computes the door and raises a card when it cannot decide. No running round switches path.",
  "Done, tests. An external two-way task with an approved list builds first (`door: external two-way builds first`, fail-first); an external task with no approved list waits on a captain card naming the reason (`door: no list asks the captain`, fail-first); a spec with no door on any project waits on a card (`door: missing door asks the captain`, fail-first); a diff path no list classifies raises a card naming the path (`door: unclassified path asks the captain`, fail-first); a base-list path forces one-way on every project and a project cannot remove it (`door: base list applies to every project`, fail-first).",
  "Docs. The firstmate and worker skills and design.md describe the per-project lists and the cannot-decide cards in a few lines."
 ],
 "explain": {
  "en": {
   "intent": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "Each project has its own approved sensitive list on top of a shared base list."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "An external task follows its door in the steps firstmate owns."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "A task whose door cannot be decided waits on a captain card."
    }
   ],
   "why": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "The captain wants every project, not only this one, to have two paths."
    }
   ],
   "scope_in": [
    "project config",
    "pins",
    "the worker launcher",
    "the gates",
    "cards"
   ],
   "scope_out": [
    "company reviewers",
    "external CI"
   ],
   "done": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "Intent 1: a test shows a base-list path is one-way on every project."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "Intent 2: a test shows an external two-way task builds first."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "Intent 3: tests show each cannot-decide case raises a card."
    }
   ],
   "notes": [
    {
     "kind": "note",
     "text": "You approve the sensitive list of each project once."
    }
   ],
   "before_nodes": [
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "External task"
    },
    {
     "state": "gone",
     "label": "Always full path"
    },
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "Merge card"
    }
   ],
   "after_nodes": [
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "External task"
    },
    {
     "state": "new",
     "label": "Path by door or ask"
    },
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "Merge card"
    }
   ]
  },
  "zh-TW": {
   "intent": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "每個專案除了共用基本清單，還有自己核准過的敏感清單。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "外部任務在 firstmate 自己管的步驟依 door 分流。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "無法判定 door 的任務停下來，開卡問船長。"
    }
   ],
   "why": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "船長要求所有專案都有兩條流程，不只本 repo。"
    }
   ],
   "scope_in": [
    "專案設定",
    "pin",
    "worker 啟動器",
    "gate",
    "卡片"
   ],
   "scope_out": [
    "公司的 reviewer",
    "外部 CI"
   ],
   "done": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "意圖 1：測試證明基本清單的路徑在每個專案都是 one-way。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "意圖 2：測試證明外部 two-way 任務直接實作。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "意圖 3：測試證明每種無法判定的情況都會開卡。"
    }
   ],
   "notes": [
    {
     "kind": "note",
     "text": "每個專案的敏感清單由你核准一次。"
    }
   ],
   "before_nodes": [
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "外部任務"
    },
    {
     "state": "gone",
     "label": "一律完整流程"
    },
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "合併卡"
    }
   ],
   "after_nodes": [
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "外部任務"
    },
    {
     "state": "new",
     "label": "依 door 分流或問船長"
    },
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "合併卡"
    }
   ]
  }
 }
}
